Bound optional executor startup and retain thread exclusions

A remote executor that connects but stalls during instruction discovery
can hold up a local thread. Give readiness and AGENTS.md discovery one
shared ten-second deadline. With an implicitly selected local primary,
exclude secondaries that cannot finish.
Explicitly selected executors must complete within the same deadline.
Native Pending-owner deferred startup is preserved.

Keep excluded executors unavailable across configuration updates, resume,
and child inheritance, including capability roots and MCP authority.
Persist them in Saffron's auxiliary database; ephemeral threads retain
only in-memory state. Copying history without that database does not
transfer exclusions. Complete admission reads feed the ordinary first
instruction load, preserving its ordering, trust and byte budget; later
refreshes remain live. Pinned reviewer snapshots avoid new discovery.
